From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:39:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scheme: a SIGKILLed caller cancels its request, and a killed
 thread starts none (issue #401)

After nc exits in a devsh session, the next command line was lost. nc
stdin thread is SIGKILLed while it reads the pty:

- If it was already blocked, UserInner::call returned EINTR without a
  Cancel, and ptyd handed the next line to the dead request. Now the
  Cancel is sent first.
- If the kill came just before call_inner blocked, the kill found the
  thread runnable and woke nothing, and the thread then slept until
  ptyd answered with the next line, which was lost with the thread
  (Pi row 397: reply of 48 bytes for a caller being killed). Now
  call_inner checks being_sigkilled under the context lock before it
  blocks and returns EINTR without sending anything.

Munmap keeps the old behaviour in both places: an exiting thread unmaps
scheme memory while tearing down, and that must reach the scheme.
---
 src/scheme/user.rs | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/scheme/user.rs b/src/scheme/user.rs
index d91ae0ab..5a2d8c5c 100644
--- a/src/scheme/user.rs
+++ b/src/scheme/user.rs
@@ -232,9 +232,22 @@ impl UserInner {
     ) -> Result<Response> {
         {
             let current_context = context::current();
-            current_context
-                .write(token.token())
-                .block("UserInner::call");
+            {
+                let mut context = current_context.write(token.token());
+                // A SIGKILL that came before this point found the thread
+                // runnable and had nothing to wake; blocking now would sleep
+                // until the scheme answers, and that answer (for ptyd the
+                // next typed line) is then lost (issue #401). The kill sets
+                // being_sigkilled under this lock, so checking here closes
+                // the window: nothing is sent yet, so nothing needs a Cancel.
+                // Munmap is left out: an exiting thread unmaps scheme memory
+                // while it tears down its address space, and that must reach
+                // the scheme.
+                if context.being_sigkilled && sqe.opcode != Opcode::Munmap as u8 {
+                    return Err(Error::new(EINTR));
+                }
+                context.block("UserInner::call");
+            }
             {
                 let mut states = self.states.lock(token.token());
                 states[sqe.tag as usize] = State::Waiting {
@@ -336,7 +349,16 @@ impl UserInner {
                                 callee_responsible,
                             };
 
-                            maybe_eintr?;
+                            // A caller that is being SIGKILLed (for example a
+                            // thread of an exiting process) still cancels the
+                            // request, so the scheme drops it. Otherwise ptyd
+                            // hands the next line typed to the dead reader and
+                            // it is lost (issue #401). Munmap keeps the old
+                            // behaviour: no Cancel, so the scheme still unmaps
+                            // while an exiting thread tears down its memory.
+                            if maybe_eintr.is_err() && sqe.opcode == Opcode::Munmap as u8 {
+                                return maybe_eintr;
+                            }
 
                             // We do not want to preempt between sending the
                             // cancellation and blocking again where we might
@@ -360,6 +382,8 @@ impl UserInner {
                                 token.token(),
                             );
 
+                            maybe_eintr?;
+
                             // 1. If cancellation was requested and arrived
                             // before the scheme processed the request, an
                             // acknowledgement will be sent back after the
